{:edb/db-before-t 1616 :edb/db-after-t 1617 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534929 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:44:06.482Z" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186158864 1078 #edb/ref 17592186158866 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444651 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444652 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444653 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186162067 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444650 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186162277 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186162277 1071 "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.75$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n Find $\\text{Var}[3X+2Y].$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186162277 1071 "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n| $x$$1$$2$$3$$f(x)$$0.2$$0.3$$0.5$ |  | $y$$1$$2$$f(y)$$0.25$$0.75$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n\nFind $Var[3X + 2Y]$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139534929 17592186045417 false] [17592186162277 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.2+2\\cdot 0.3+3\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.2+4\\cdot 0.3+9\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =5.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5.9-{2.3}^{2} \\\\  & =0.61.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 0.75 \\\\  & =1.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.25+4\\cdot 0.75 \\\\  & =3.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =3.25-{1.75}^{2} \\\\  & =0.1875.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-2Y] & ={3}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & ={3}^{2}(0.61)+{2}^{2}(0.1875) \\\\  & =6.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444625 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444654 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444625 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444655 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444625 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444656 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444625 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444657 13194139