7 true] [17592186444649 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444635 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444649 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444638 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444649 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444649 1077 "selection" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444649 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444638 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444649 1079 #uuid "e9075f10-8356-5116-9d8d-9363c1194e5f" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444650 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444648 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444650 1069 "q-129540" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444650 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444650 1071 "Consider two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=8,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=11$\nand second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=70$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=130.$ Find the variance of  $4X-\\frac{1}{3}Y.$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444650 1072 #uuid "10f2f9d4-7d62-5e91-afc7-8a268909f88f" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444650 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =70-{8}^{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =130-{11}^{2} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[4X-\\frac{1}{3}Y] & ={4}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =16\\cdot 6+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444651 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444647 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444651 1069 "q-129525" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444651 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444651 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=100$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=200.$ Find $\\text{Var}[0.5X+0.4Y].$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444651 1072 #uuid "4592eee9-4d66-541e-b103-0104f487a3d0" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444651 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[0.5X+0.4Y]={0.5}^{2}\\cdot 100+{0.4}^{2}\\cdot 200=57.\n$$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444652 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444646 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444652 1069 "q-129526" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444652 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444652 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=20$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y].$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444652 1072 #uuid "4ebe566e-595e-53c5-acba-b32f38c7b929" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444652 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y]={(0.5)}^{2}\\cdot 20+{(-2)}^{2}\\cdot 5=25.\n$$" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444653 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444649 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444653 1069 "q-129524" 13194139534929 17592186045417 true] [17592186444653 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534929 1759